 "evidence": "One session on sp1, ABBA: the PR's bench_sparse_mla_pipeline.py on both images (bench-*.json; CUDA-graph replay of 10 back-to-back plan.run per graph, 25 windows, arms run one after another), then our h964.py: the image's SparseMlaV41Plan and the bench's embedded stage-1 kernel on the bench's workload with seeded inputs, graph replay interleaved window by window (25 windows), output hashes compared across images and arms.",
 "readme_command_defects": [
  "The README gives no command for its benchmark; we ran the script's own argparse interface (--output, --boot)",
  "The bench labels the image's kernel 'base_1107' and compares it with its own embedded copy of the candidate (make_candidate_sparse_mla). On the candidate image that arm is the shipped 0769 kernel, so running the bench there compares candidate with candidate; the image-level comparison is the base arm across images",
  "The embedded copy is not the shipped code: it computes h0 outside the segment-active branch and renames the record-segment local, and runs 0.4..1.2 us faster than the shipped kernel at decode M=12..24 (bit-identical output). The PR's decode deltas at those M are partly the copy's"
 ],
